criteria.notes:
Grounding and provenance now hold on every channel the iteration-2 review named:
- text quotes must be present and aligned to whole numbers for every field;
- a deadline's time must be in its quote;
- image provenance is limited to the four product fields;
- the ledger charges the cap for every killed started call.

The residuals each have a decision and an owner:
- the deadline's date part and the Arabic am/pm markers (dec-mv36cgyj-01f0741d);
- lexical grounding (dec-mv36ch5t-01a1d509);
- capacity and diameter from the photo (SEC-D-14, carry item 6);
- SIGKILL and the runner's SIGHUP (FU-28).

The full suite, the eval, NFR5 and the browser suite are green, and artifact coverage is complete.

resolvedFindings.resolution:
Resolved; this is also security's SEC-D-11. d1's validateExtraction requires the quote to have at least one occurrence aligned to whole numbers (schema.js L306, L349-L372). Before a quote that starts with a digit or separator, there may be no digit, and no separator preceded by a digit; the same holds after a quote that ends in one. Clock times are masked before numbers are read (L333-L336). d3 inherits the rule through quoteGrounded, so there is a single source.

The conditions:
- the alignment rule is as I asked;
- the P3b cases are unknown through the route: my P3b re-run by path (ev:ev-mv36npp3-01cc274c) shows cupQuantity 200 from '1,200 cups', lidQuantity 200 from '1200 lids' and capacityMl 50 from '250 ml' unknown, while diameter 90 stays known;
- '250' from '2500 cups' is refused in d1's suite (schema.test.js L227) and in my P7;
- the SEC-7 route test extract.test.js L436 covers 200 from '1,200';
- '1,200 cups'->1200, '250ml'->250, '$120.50'->120.5 and '٢٥٠ مل'->250 stay known in P7 (ev:ev-mv36n2by-01c422d2).

Mutants M15, M16, M17 and M18 are killed (ev:ev-mv36sh0c-019c0ced). A space as thousands separator still grounds; that is lexical and covered by dec-mv36ch5t-01a1d509 (TR-D-8).
